Hi - a question, for those more knowledgable than I...

The Alpha motherboards made before the LX164's  (Aspen called
them "Durango") had either a 128bit or 256bit access path,
depending on whether or not you filled all the SIMM slots.
Maybe ten months ago, I remember some postings about not
getting good performance out of it unless you filled all the slots.

The new ones (LX's) seem to only have the 128bit option,
e.g., fewer slots, gotta use bigger SDRAMS.   Does this incur
a performance penalty, or is there some other factor at work?

If anybody has actually measured these three things against
each other... or really understands how this all works...
your advice/info would be appreciated!

Thanks,

Lev Gelb







