> Vivo sound card
> 3c590 3com network card
> 12x scsi cdrom drive
> 
> My partitions are as such:
> 
> 1 gb Linux swap

Could it be that Linux cannot handle a 1 gb swap partition ?
On PCs the maximum is 128 Mb. As I understand it, Linux uses a bitfield
in one page (4 Kb on PC, 8 Kb on Alpha) to indicate which pages of
swap it uses.

On a PC, this gives you a bitfield of 32K entries to pages of 4K, thus
the maximum of 128 Mb.
For the alpha, this would be 64K entries to pages of 8K, thus 512Mb.

I don't know whether this is your problem (or even correct), but perhaps
it helps helps.

Martin


