You are right that you can purchase a license for VMS itself, but 3rd Party vendors are
not allowed to implement the necessary PAL-Codes in their BIOS to actually run this
softwares. You only get this by buying a original DEC-Machine. Usually they don't even
implement it in their mainboards that go out ot OEMs. This results in the situation, that
a standard PC164 from an OEM can't run it, but a similar PC164based DEC Machine can...

I really like these buisiness people from DEC...

