A question to those who've upgraded their cache from 256K to something more
realistic (say 1M). What sort of performance increase do you see, on a
benchmark we've all suffered (!), say kernel compilation or running emacs? I
think a lot of the complaints about the Multia's speed may actually be
complaints about insufficient cache. When I do numerical stuff on the Multia
I'm pleasantly surprised by the speed I can squeeze out of it, despite gcc.

Another question: how many people have successfully upclocked the 066 in
their Multia, and got away with it? I would imagine 166MHz -> 200MHz would
be safe, considering the 233MHz variety can be upclocked to 266MHz without
trouble. Presumably this is a lot safer than upclocking, e.g., a StrongARM
which tends to die after a few days when pushed from 200MHz to 280MHz,
despite not even getting warm.

