Lower cost, yes, by a long shot.  Easier to set up, depends on who you 
are.  Slower than SCSI, yes, by a long shot, especially when you're 
talking about bus-mastering which IDE has never been able to handle quite 
right.  *You* might not see a reason for going with SCSI, but people with 
real work that needs to get done certainly see the need.  To each his/her 
own.

