besien@solair1.inter.nl.net (Krist van Besien) writes:
> So I can't enter any commands, can't boot Linux.
> 
> Data: Redhat 4.1, Linload 1.3, Noname board, with a French keyboard
> that the ARC console doesn't have any troubel with.

Blame me for that one.  The keyboard driver in MILO is *extremely*
simpleminded; it uses a polled interface and a hard-coded keycode
table... I bunged it together in about two hours a couple years back
when I got the *VERY* first MILO from Dave Rusling.  It had *no*
command interface, no way to pass options, and a hard-coded boot
sequence.  I decided that simply wouldn't do and added the command
interface and keyboard driver.

There is a workaround in your case, though.  When you load MILO
via ARC console, the "OSLOADOPTIONS" string associated with that
particular boot option is passed to MILO as the first command
to execute.  Normally this is set to "debug" or "nodebug" by the
ARC console when you set up the boot option.  Simply replace this
string with the boot command you would have typed at MILO.

