I too got burned by how incredibly bad the documentation was.  At one point
in the process I got stuck at the same point you're at, in my case the reason
for the panic was that MILO makes absolutely no attempt whatever to size the
RAM on a Noname, it just blindly assumes that they all have 24 MB.  So if you
have less then you'll run into NXM while loading the RAM disk.  My machine
has 16 MB, so for me the fix was to "setenv MEMORY_SIZE 16" at the MILO
prompt, then it passes the correct size to Linux and all is well.

John Wilson
D Bit



