I actually have had the same problem on ocassion.  I found only two ways
to make it work. 

1) I got kernel modules working and made the ne2000 driver a module then
added the appropriate information to /etc/conf.modules and viola it
worked.

2) The first time I installed I was having alot of trouble with the
modules and the milo param ether= was not working as I am sure you can
attest.  So I had to actually hard code the ne2000 driver.  I actually
only added 3 lines to the drivers/net/ne.c and it worked.  Here they are:

line 381 of ne.c should be something like:
	 dev->irq = 9;

add this afterwards until you get modules working:
	if(!dev->irq){      /*HACK added to get my card to work*/
	   dev->irq = YOURIRQ;
	}

and recompile and it should work.  This is the only way that I have been
able to get mine to work in the early stages of setting the box up.


