In article <3448e191.9335164@news.hol.fr>, EmmanuelS <EmmanuelS@hol.fr> wrote:
>I would like to know if Dec C++ is same than Gnu C++ from linux Alpha?
>
>If no what is the difference?

DEC CXX is NOT the same as G++ for linux/alpha, no, not at all, not
remotely.

When I tried DEC CXX 5.0 and compared the resulting code to G++,
the G++ code was 2x as fast, and compiled more quickly, with both
compilers at their highest optimization levels.

DEC CXX is a commercial product, while g++ is free, so the clear superiority
of g++ wass shocking.  You'd think DEC would make a good C++ compiler.

The best C++ compiler I've seen for Alpha is the KAI KCC compiler,
which uses DEC's very good optimizing C compiler on Alpha/OSF.  So
far as I know, that compiler is not available on Linux/Alpha.

PeterM



