mdprod01@uctvms.uct.ac.za wrote:

> I want to install linux on my Pentium 233, under DOS or windows95. Could
> someone advice me how to have access to linux, is there a site where I can
> download it? I am in Cape Town, South Africa.

There are several so-called "Distributions". The most popular are probably
RedHat, Slackware and Debian. You can either purchase a CDROM paying with
your credit card, and it will cost you around $50 with the shipment to
South Africa (look at http://www.cdrom.com or http://www.redhat.com for more
details). Otherwise, try one of the many Linux sites and download the
distribution from the Internet, for instance from:
ftp://nic.funet.fi/pub/Linux/images. Slackware is probably the best suited to
download from the net because it is splited in packages of 1.44 Mb that fit
in a DOS diskette and the names are adapted to the prehistoric DOS file name
convention (see Slackware/slakware under the previous directory).

Good Luck!

