> PLEASE, note that I want to know about IDE (vs. SCSI) on a pc164
> Alpha, not about generic comparisons!

500 mhz PC164 256M ram IDE

time dd if=/dev/zero of=foo bs=1024k count=100   (100 megabyte file)
60 seconds elapsed time, 28% cpu usage (and much of the rest of the system
consumed by "update")

time cp foo bar
120 seconds elapsed time, 35% usage (and much...)

200 mhz dual PPro 256M ram SCSI (440FX chipset motherboard)

dd takes 4 seconds, 88% cpu
cp takes 30 seconds, 14% cpu

Note for the dd that it probably hadn't flushed all the blocks to disk
before the command finished. In both cases cp should have found most
of the blocks to be read in the disk cache.

I don't have an IDE PPro system to see if the PPro has this same problem,
nor a SCSI PC164 to verify that it doesn't have this problem. I am rather
startled by the result.

-- g



