several questions come to mind.  first, does hdparm exist for Alpha Linux,
and are you using sensible settings such as -m8c3d1?  next, the standard
questions what disk, and what about the filesystem, virgin, with 4k blocks?
also, why not use a file that's larger than dram, so that you don't end
up mainly measuring the buffer cache?  also, I expect that you'd get better
performance by merely using a reasonable buffer size, not one that
necessarily flushes all cache...


