: dd takes 4 seconds, 88% cpu
: cp takes 30 seconds, 14% cpu

88% is an excellent indicator that you're measuring buffer-cache.

: nor a SCSI PC164 to verify that it doesn't have this problem. I am rather
: startled by the result.

really?  in what sense?  it's basically impossible to interpret numbers
that are so confounded.  why not simply post a bonnie run?


anyway, getting back to the issue: I can't imagine any reason why
busmastering ATA wouldn't work quite fine on Alphas.  I _can_ imagine
that PIO (any port io, actually) might be peculiar and possibly slow,
but busmastering ATA on x86's is quite sweet:
~5% CPU overhead, ~10 MB/s sustained.

