BULLSHIT.  this is the worst of urban legends.  busmastering ATA has 
been ubiquitous for 3 years.  busmastered ATA has, if anything, _lower_
CPU overhead than SCSI, simply because the protocol is vastly simpler
and requires far less host-target interaction.

if you don't believe me, measure it.  I have, and will provide numbers
if you're actually interested.



