Well, I've had luck with getting dhcpcd-0.65 to run on my UDB. However, it
generates a bunch of unaligned accesses every now and then, but if you can
ignore that it seems to work well. The only gotcha is that when you unpack
the source tree and do make clean, it doesn't erase the binary, just the
object files. So if you have em86 installed and don't delete the binary
that it comes with, it will attempt to run it and stumble. 

If that fails, a friend of mine has worked most of the unaligned accesses
out of the program and managed to get it to work with 2.1 kernels on
Intel. It seems to work fine, except that it bombs out when used with 2.1
on an Alpha. It should even compile and run (theoretically) under
SPARCLinux and other 64-bit systems which it dodn't previously work.
Hopefully this will be ready for release soon.


