You've discovered that the machine uses one DB25 for both serial ports.
The pinout can be found at
<http://www.brouhaha.com/~eric/computers/udb.html> and other places.

> Also I notied that MILO doesnt like it if I have the modem on while its
> running.  It seams that whenever i type on the keyboard, it makes the
> modem lights blink and complains of unknown commands from nowhere.  Is
> this to be expected?

It does that. What you're seeing is the console echo on serial 1. 

I could not get my USR 28.8 to work at all on serial 1, but I was using
a 26 conductor cable (shell ground y'know) so perhaps some of the lines
from serial 2 were interfereing with little known alternate pins on the
USR. What I did was to make a Y cable to breakout the two serial lines
and put my modem on serial port 2 (cua1). Now I have no problems.

Y cables are available from Starship for $25.00 or so but I was in a
hurry.

Good luck,

Charles



