compiling
> > with gcc or g77. Or is there a need for buying a commercial compiler to 
reach
> > full performance of an Alpha chip?
> 
> Gcc/g77 are quite still very slow (in relative terms) on the Alpha.

One of the reasons g77 leads to slow executables on Alpha is the inability of 
the (current) backend to deal efficiently with array index calculations which 
use half words (which is the default case if you're just using Fortran 
programs with ordinary INTEGERs as array indices).

We are working on that problem.

A (non-supported) way of temporarily (i.e. until the *real* problem is fixed) 
work-around this shortcoming is setting the preprocessor name 
FFECOM_FASTER_ARRAY_REFS to 1 instead of 0 in f/com.c.  This will make the 
Fortran frontend spell out the array indexing computation to the code 
generation phase, which happens to work around the "subword index" problem.

However, use at your own risk !

