Marko Vendelin wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> I am installing Alpha PC164 with "generic" ne2000 compatible
> network card. Unfortunately, the system (Linux)
> detects it occasionaly: once everything works, the next time
> it doesn't. IRQs are not conflicting.
> 
> My card is PCI NE2000. Does anybody fixed this problem?
> 
> --
> Marko Vendelin,
> e-mail: markov@ioc.ee

Hi,

I've found a solution for my problem in Ethernet HowTo. Namely,
if PCI NE2000 card is not detected by kernel, then IRQ, I/O address
could be specified in milo as follows:

boot hda3:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda3 ether=11,0x300,eth0

where NE2000 card uses irq 11, i/o address 0x300.

Happy linuxing,

-- 
